          "text": "General appearance"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Well appearing, comfortable, not toxic, and not jaundiced."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Abdominal examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Abdomen soft with mild generalised lower abdominal tenderness, left greater than right. No rebound, guarding, rigidity, focal right or left iliac fossa peritonism, epigastric or right upper quadrant tenderness, masses, or organomegaly. Bowel sounds normal."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Cardiovascular and respiratory examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Heart sounds dual with no murmur. Chest clear."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-14",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Brief genitourinary examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No costovertebral angle tenderness or obvious external hernia. Testes non-tender with no swelling."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-15",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-15",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported toenail changes"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Thick yellow toenails present for a couple of years, slowly increasing and mainly affecting the great toes. Nails are crumbly; the patient keeps them trimmed and finds the appearance embarrassing in thongs. No current pain, redness, swelling, or discharge. Intermittently tried over-the-counter athlete's foot cream; has not used nail lacquer. Patient wonders whether this may be from work showers."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-16",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-16",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Toenail examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Both hallux nails yellow-brown and thickened with distal involvement of approximately 40-50% on the right and 30-40% on the left. Some subungual debris and mild onycholysis. Other toenails mildly involved, less than 20%."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-17",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-17",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Periungual skin and foot examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No surrounding erythema, warmth, or swelling. No obvious tinea pedis today."
      }
    },
